  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The expression for the Freundlich isotherm can be represented by the following equation</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></msub><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow></msup></math></p><p>Taking log on both sides</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>log</mi><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>logk</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mfrac><mi>logP</mi></math></p><p>On comparing with given equation of straight line, we get</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>505</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>logK</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>505</mn></math></p><p>So, the answer is 3 and 2.505</p>"
  }
